==Battleground==
*3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 133.33~136.67 seconds<sup>4,000f~4,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*10 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 533.33 seconds<sup>16,000f</sup>, delay 2~5.33 seconds<sup>60f~160f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Kappy Kawano]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Golem Sunfish]] spawns.
**2 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**2 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Gabriel]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
**12 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Kappy Jr.]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main difficulty of the stage stems from Golem Sunfish freezing, cursing and damaging your units at extreme range while the Kappys deal heavy damage and spam [[Surge Attack|Surges]], alongside money management, even making killing Celeboodle with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and/or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] a priority to keep your funds up. Obviously you would want [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune attackers]] that can get by even under fire from Golem Sunfish for this particular stage.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]]: Essentially a requirement for this stage, being the most accessible Surge-immune meatshield makes him the prime pick for a meatshield for all strategies. Albeit vulnerable to Golem Sunfish, he still serves as filler for your other defensive units.
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]]: An amazing anti-Surge meatshield that's spammable, has great bulk to survive a few hits from the incoming [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] peons and can deal good damage against Kawano and the peons themselves.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can requires all the Talents you might have at this point (besides Target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]), abusing its high damage to quickly remove strong peons like Sir Rel, Relic Doge, Celeboodle (for additional resources), Gabriel and Angelic Gory. Can Can is also pretty tough, able to survive at least one of the Surges while being knocked back, which allows it to get a successful hit in and change the whole course of battle.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Mainly to take out Celeboodle quickly for a huge boost to cash, and chip against the bosses.
*Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]]: With Surge Immunity and other Talents such as [[Survive]] and [[Mini-Wave]], this unit is notable for being able to outrange Kawano and deal stackable DPS against him, though he needs a lot of investment and + levels to be a viable choice if the player doesn't have good Uber Rares.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: Even despite Hitman having no Surge Immunity, Kawano has a lot of downtime between his attacks, which allows Hitman to get in and deal an insane amount of burst damage onto Kawano. He can also work against Kappy Jr., but his lack of Surge Immunity makes Hitman risky against him.
*[[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]]: A very bulky unit with good DPS against Traitless. Unlike Hitman, he leans towards the more defensive side with his [[Strong]] ability, though do note he is still vulnerable to Surges.
*[[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]: Ape Lord Luza gets a notable mention thanks to its combination of abilities, with Curse and Surge Immunity as well as massive damage and resistance to Relics. Luza's high stats and range allows it to consistently hit the Kappy variants, while its resistance means Golem Sunfish will not be able to destroy it quickly. Lower-ranged Relic peons that walk into the line of fire are immediately reduced to oblivion when the attack hits, and since Luza's Long Distance hits up to 550 range with essentially no blind spot, it can even potentially snipe them. Once the Kappys are gone, Luza remains useful in fighting Golem Sunfish as it's usually one of the last threats remaining.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]: If you've managed to beat the final floor of the [[Infernal Tower/Floor 50|Infernal Tower]] before Kappy Kawano, Esoteric Uril's kit is insanely helpful here; being able to beat up the Relic peons, dealing good DPS with his Surge, having a low cooldown and even sniping Golem Sunfish at times makes him a good pick for this stage. Despite his surges generating a bunch of Counter-Surge from Kawano, this is mainly irrelevant considering how you're supposed to bring Immune to Surge attackers anyways.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]]: He can help deal with the Golem Sunfish and incoming Relic peons with his freeze and piercing Surge for Golem, but do note that his Surge can also cause a Counter-Surge from Kawano. Ideally, he should be in [[True Form]] for the Knockback to push Golem Sunfish back.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Jelly Dumpling's level 7 Wave makes it one of the few consistent ways of hitting Golem Sunfish in the back. As the peons tend to spawn a bit frequently while Kawano has a somewhat long attack cycle, Jelly Dumpling does have some opportunities to shine by crippling peons and getting some chip damage. Its Normal and Evolved Forms are not recommended due to their slower speed and lower range.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Boulder may cause Kappy Kawano to generate multiple Surges, but its extreme health and Surge Immunity mean that when boosted by Research [[Cat Combo|Combos]], it can be a great source of defense by walling the nasty peons, and its [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]] prevents Golem Sunfish from disabling it. Stone should not be used alone, but it does greatly assist with meatshielding.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]]: He's great at tanking any of Kappy Kawano or Kappy Jr.'s attacks, though he will be shredded in seconds if sent out with Sir Rel or Angelic Gory on the field. As long as you can deal with the peons, he will be a good choice.
*[[Calligraphy Cat (Rare Cat)|Tea Master Cat]]: With Research Combos, this fairly obscure unit can be used as a ranged meatshield against Kappy Jr, and is able to tank hits from Golem Sunfish with his Strong vs. Relics ability.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]]: Though he must be timed properly, he is a great choice for crowd-control against both Kappys, If combined with Boulder Cat and Metal Macho, they can pretty much control the level.
*[[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]]: Jiangshi Cat has the [[Tiny Ancient Hunt (Combo)|Tiny Ancient Hunt Combo]] with Li'l King Dragon Cat, and also makes for good extra defense with his guaranteed Survive and high speed (with Talents). He should only be summoned with an excess of money though, since he's a large cash drain.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Most [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusives work well here, as they are powerful against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless Enemies]] and thus can resolve the Kappys; however, you need to ensure their effects are not interfered by Curse if they aren't immune to it. Also note whether any of them are Immune to Surges or not, as lacking Surge Immunity means they won't last long to make a major impact. The only exception to this is [[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]], which makes up it's lack of Surge Immunity with a fast recharge.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]: His extreme damage and Immunity to Surges allow him to cripple Kappy Jr. Against Kappy Kawano, Lasvoss requires some timing to sneak an attack in. His combo, [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Bad Guys]], is also helpful to spam Boulder Cat and other units more.
*[[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Lucifer]]: If you have decent amount of anti-Surge units to evade the Counter-Surges, Lucifer will be a great generalist who can outrange the majority of enemies, whilst enduring the attack of Golem Sunfish thanks to his Strong ability, which can also be boosted with Cat Cactus.
*[[Ultra Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]]: With investment, Klay can be immune to every Surge, [[Curse]], and [[Freeze]] dealt by any enemy in the stage, and will only attack Traitless enemies, making him a great unit to quickly dispatch of the Kappys. His health and range also keep him safe from the Sir Rels, and he can easily tank Golem Sunfish, allowing him to stick around long enough to make a huge difference, as each hit from a level 60 Klay will take a huge chunk out of the Kappy duo's health.
*[[Ultra Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Anubis]]: When Ultra Talented he can one-shot all of the peons and melt the Kappys, being a great counter to this stage. He has Surge Immunity for the main threats and can be Talented to add his own Surge Attack—though make sure you're prepared for the Counter-Surge. With enough Surge Immune units, you can wipe out a chunk of the peons and deal heavy damage to the Kappy. He also has enough bulk to tank the Golem Sunfish, but be wary of his long foreswing animation and three knockbacks.
*[[Giyu Tomioka (Uber Rare Cat)|Giyu Tomioka]]: His Immunity to Curse and Surge make him largely effective against both Kappys and the Relic peons, and along with his Strong Against Traitless and a guaranteed Slow, he can control the duo and prevent them from pushing properly. However, Golem Sunfish and the peons can chip him down if improperly protected.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]: Kozuchimaru's Immunity to Surges and Massive Damage to Traitless allows them to quickly deal large amounts of damage to both Kappys without having to worry about getting juggled by the constant Surges the stage contains. Watch out for Golem Sunfish however, as its Curse can massively reduce Kozuchimaru's damage output.

==Trivia==
*"Ghost" is a translation of 妖怪 ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'', a class of supernatural creatures and phenomena in Japanese folklore. The ''[[wikipedia:Kappa (folklore)|kappa]]'' is an example of a ''yōkai''.
*Ghost King Finale is the first and currently only [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] to include two different [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]].

